      "id": "b2e8c76afe24da1bb8cfc71513692ed7",
      "title": "What Ukraine Hath Wrought: Lessons for War, If We\u2019re Listening",
      "summary": "<p>Four years into Russia&#8217;s war against Ukraine, what should the U.S. military have learned by now? Michael Kofman (Carnegie Endowment), Dara Massicot (Carnegie Endowment), and Amos Fox (Arizona State University) join Ryan to discuss. The easy answer is drones and AI, but our guests argue the harder truths lie elsewhere: &#8220;Old-fashioned&#8221; ideas like campaigning, holding territory, mass, and attrition still decide wars. And, as they discuss, based on U.S. performance in the war with Iran, it may be that not much learning has happened at all.Image: ArmyInform</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://warontherocks.com/what-ukraine-hath-wrought-lessons-for-war-if-were-listening/\">What Ukraine Hath Wrought: Lessons for War, If We&#8217;re Listening</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://warontherocks.com\">War on the Rocks</a>.</p>",
